From 124446cb7d20a421444cdf9cd7ffa9abc2c243b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 08:50:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 136/174] feat: the Sandbox viewport chooses who drives the
 picture while editing (cinecam editor preview)

Plugin side of decisions/s9-editor-cinecam-preview.md. Until now "active" for the cinematic
camera meant the CryDefaultEntities camera manager's pointer, which in edit mode is simply the
last camera component that initialised on level load - so the editor picture followed whichever
camera happened to be last, not the one the viewport showed, and the game-only effects were
skipped outright while editing.

- Interface/ICineCamEditorPreview.h + exported CryGetCineCamEditorPreview(): the level-editor
  viewport tells the plugin once per rendered frame what it is looking through (Default, CineCam,
  or a camera entity). Frame-counter staleness (two frames), never wall clock, because the editor
  skips frames when idle.
- Edit-mode resolver (UpdateEditorPreview): Entity -> that entity's cinematic camera drives the
  full effect set, including the formerly game-only half (FinalizeGameCamera split into the
  view write, still game-only, and ApplyGameOnlyEffects) and DOF with the entity's own focus
  (CanApplyViewEffects replaces the seven !IsEditing() gates); an entity without a cinematic
  camera (plain camera, TrackView) degrades to Default. CineCam -> a plugin-owned publisher with
  no entity: scene referred on, default ODT, sun shafts suppressed, exposure from the shared
  histogram meter only (aperture/shutter/ISO/ND do not participate), one knob cinecam_EditorLookEV.
  Default -> nobody publishes; the stock picture.
- Hand-over order: the outgoing owner restores before the incoming one latches, so
  Entity -> CineCam -> Default leaves stock state. Ctrl+G either way drops the baselines
  (ResetPostEffects runs on both edges) and the viewport re-establishes the preview next frame.
- Shared code lifted out of the component into CineCamShared.* (meter reduction, adaptation,
  scene-referred convention, LUT publication); the component's game-mode behaviour is unchanged.
- One log line per owner change: "[cinecam] editor preview -> ...".

Naming: the plugin's abbreviation is cinecam from here on; existing ccam_ cvars keep their names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
